VU1 interpreter and GS rasterizer speedups for 3D scenes (dotr-recomp issue #13); output is bit-identical.

VU1: FMAC flags take a float fast path (a round-to-zero result strictly inside (FLT_MIN, FLT_MAX), and for
ACC +/- product no heavy cancellation, only sets S) instead of recomputing every lane in long double; the decoded
pair is used by reference; the hazard scan is skipped once every register is ready (global and per-VF maxima);
XGKICK copies a qword with memcpy and no longer zeroes its 64 KiB buffer on each kick or program start; upper NOPs
skip operand normalization; commits only clear `valid`; free flag/VF slots come from the occupancy masks.

GS: small sprites/triangles, previously drawn one by one on the caller thread, are queued (up to 1024) and drawn
in one row-band-parallel pass. Every other backend entry point flushes the queue first, as does a primitive whose
texture overlaps a queued frame/Z buffer (or whose buffers overlap a queued texture), or a change in rounding mode.
GS::processGIFPacket/writeRegister flush on return unless GS::setDeferredRaster(true); the runtime enables it
because it reads VRAM only through GS methods (tests that read the VRAM buffer directly keep the old contract).

